{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Rubber grommets, acrylic panels and wide washers fit my recent drilling and fastening purchases because they help me assemble panels and protect wires passing through them.",
    "The inch-size bolt assortment complements my metric kits and UNC rivet nuts, while duct tape and quick glue cover repair jobs that my existing adhesives handle less conveniently."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Printer resin does not fit my casting epoxy use: it requires equipment I have not shown any need for. The rain-barrel fitting likewise assumes a water-container project I do not currently have.",
    "Another infrared thermometer duplicates a recent purchase. The height gauge interests me, but my existing caliper meets my immediate measuring needs, so interest alone would not make me choose it today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Sharing a material name such as resin does not mean two products serve the same task or work with the same equipment.",
    "Buying workshop tools does not mean I need every kind of repair fitting or another version of a tool I recently acquired."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Useful additions fill gaps in my supplies: compatible inch fasteners, pressure-spreading washers and wire-protecting grommets add functions to what I already own.",
    "The purpose of an item matters more than a shared name: rubber wiring grommets complement my eyelet equipment, whereas another infrared thermometer repeats an existing function."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my workshop and fabrication interests, but sometimes confused useful complements with duplicate tools or supplies for projects and equipment I do not have."
}"}
